@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;design] shared-sign-in-retains-the-account-page
Both hosts MUST render the existing sign-in page: the Pully heading, Google first
when available, then the email field alone and Continue revealing the test-account
password field. There MUST NOT be a sign-up action. Native Google selection dismissal
MUST leave the page signed out without an error. The supplied artwork MUST render the
canonical Pully and Google marks. Source: settings-sign-in-page, Tavi 16 Oct 12:47 and
16:52, and the accepted 21 Oct 2026 maximum-reuse Compose iOS plan.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security;architecture] shared-sign-in-input-belongs-to-its-owner
Credential inputs and pending attempts MUST belong to the services owner that opened
the page. Replacing that owner MUST discard the previous email/password input and
retire its native selection/commit authority; credentials MUST NOT use saved route
state. Native Google availability MUST require both the server audience and matching
local iOS registration. Source: Tavi's 21 Oct 2026 iOS source/account isolation plan,
client-invalidates-old-sources and the existing settings-sign-in-page contract.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security;architecture] live-account-retains-one-shared-client
The native account host MUST supply secure storage and native Google selection only;
account status, restored-session verification and sign-in/out MUST use the existing
shared Repo methods. Restored credentials MUST appear only in the verification
configuration until the server confirms the same email. An offline verification
MUST retain the saved session without publishing it as active. Source: Tavi's
21 Oct 2026 full iOS implementation request and the accepted authentication plan.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security;architecture] live-account-source-change-retires-private-routes
Every native account/server/Access identity mutation MUST synchronously retire the
old shared routes, caches, size lease and observers before publishing its replacement
connection, then notify the runtime after publication. An earlier pending operation
MUST NOT commit credentials or clear a newer account. Resume failures MUST NOT forget
an already verified account. Source: Tavi's 21 Oct 2026 source-owned native adapter
plan and ios-account-reset-invalidates-observers.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security;product] live-account-expiry-requires-session-rejection
An HTTP failure during account verification MUST expire a session only for the shared
client's typed Unauthorized error. An HTML or other invalid HTTP 401 response MUST retain
saved credentials and MUST NOT publish a restored session before verification succeeds.
An already verified account MUST remain available after that recoverable failure.
Source: Tavi's accepted 21 Oct 2026 native account/error-recovery plan and
live-account-source-change-retires-private-routes.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security;architecture] shared-server-input-and-probe-follow-the-owner
Both hosts MUST use the existing Server URL and Access fields. Unsaved Access input
MUST belong to the page's native source owner and MUST NOT enter saved route state.
An old page MUST NOT save over a replacement source. Save's explicit connection probe
MUST remain bound to the configuration just saved, without following later replacement
credentials. Native adapters MUST retain credential storage ownership. Source: the
accepted 21 Oct 2026 iOS native configuration and source-isolation plan, retaining
the existing Android ServerPage and root phone-api-one-account boundary.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security;architecture] account-status-keeps-owner-eligibility
An observed change in the server's account-enabled status MUST synchronously retire
private routes/caches and restart verification before presenting the replacement state.
A retained session MUST NOT make account settings or private analytics eligible while
the server explicitly reports no account configuration. Account RPC timing MUST reach
the host's real first-party observer, including restored-session verification. Source:
Tavi's 21 Oct 2026 same-app iOS request, preserving Android Account.noteServer and
root phone-api-one-account and analytics-stays-on-our-server.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security;architecture] account-observation-awaits-current-verification
An observation-resume waiter MUST settle against the latest source's completed
account verification and settings synchronization. Source replacement MUST wake it
without waiting for an obsolete transport reply, and cancellation of that waiter
MUST NOT cancel the runtime-owned probe. An offline retained Ready page MUST NOT
count as successful fresh verification. Source: Tavi's 21 Oct 2026 foreground/resume
iOS plan and live-account-source-change-retires-private-routes.
The scene's read owner MUST pause immediately on background/source replacement,
follow the latest verification without cancelling its runtime probe, and reject a
late foreground grant after scene stop/close. Successful sign-in, server change or
explicit retry in an already active scene MUST be able to resume current reads
without another scene transition. Source: the same accepted native lifecycle plan.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;design] shared-settings-use-the-original-choice-previews
The shared palette picker, app/code font rows and layout/code samples MUST retain
Android's real choice previews and immediate shared AppSettings updates. A selected
font MUST draw its own sample face, palette choices MUST use the existing theme wipe
and search, and a font choice MUST return through the containing sheet's callback.
Native hosts MUST use these same bodies rather than redraw parallel settings screens.
Source: settings-show-what-you-choose, settings-fonts-section, DESIGN.md rules81/126,
and Tavi's 21 Oct 2026 maximum-reuse same-app iOS decision.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security;product] shared-model-picker-cannot-act-through-a-new-owner
The actual Model/Effort picker MUST use the host's real catalog/configuration store.
A retained callback or late catalog reply MUST NOT update a replacement server/account
owner. Native kept catalogs and per-engine model memory MUST use the root's opaque
source namespace; no source's CLI account/catalog metadata MAY seed another source.
The existing engine tabs, chosen model, supported effort and immediate cached names
MUST retain their Android behavior. Source: settings-model-row-names-the-model,
client-invalidates-old-sources and Tavi's 21 Oct 2026 maximum-reuse iOS plan.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security;product] shared-account-key-pages-retire-their-private-state
Account/key pages MUST use the real shared Repo and retain the original create/list,
copy-once and revoke flows. Their forms, focus and effects MUST belong to the current
services owner. A dismissed/replaced account MUST NOT copy an old secret, perform a
new key request or accept a late key response into another owner. The host MUST clear
the old one-time key, selected key and list synchronously before publishing replacement
credentials; the one-time key MUST NOT use persisted or saved route state. Source:
settings-agent-keys-on-the-phone, client-invalidates-old-sources and Tavi's 21 Oct
2026 full shared iOS implementation request.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;security] shared-account-signout-failure-is-recoverable
A failed sign-out or native credential deletion MUST remain a visible, retryable
account-page error while the current account is retained. An active attempt MUST
not accept a duplicate tap. Cancellation, page disposal or source retirement MUST
not publish a late failure; successful local sign-out MAY retire its own services.
Source: Tavi's accepted 21 Oct 2026 native account/error-recovery plan and
android-no-dead-ends, including the actual Keychain failure boundary.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security;product] shared-stats-belongs-to-its-opening-source
The shared Stats page MUST show the same range's kept answer immediately and refresh
through the actual analytics-summary RPC. Usage stats off MUST prevent requests and
private cache reads. A retired owner, changed source or cancelled request MUST NOT
commit a late response. Replacing the services owner MUST retire the entire page's
range, chart state and producer jobs. Native summary preferences MUST use the root's
opaque eligible-account/server/Access namespace; unmarked legacy Android summaries
MUST NOT be assigned to an arbitrary private owner. Source: stats-at-once, existing
settings-usage-stats-drops-queue and Tavi's 21 Oct 2026 source-isolated same-app plan.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;design] shared-stats-preserves-usage-and-formatting
Both hosts MUST render the original Stats totals, per-day charts, feature/model AI
usage and unpriced-cost dash from one shared body. Counts and Gregorian dates MUST
use the app's chosen language; dollars, compact tokens and time units MUST retain
the existing Android formatting policy. Source: stats-ai-usage, DESIGN.md rules178/181
and Tavi's 21 Oct 2026 maximum-reuse same-app decision.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:architecture;security] shared-settings-use-one-active-source
The root MUST provide one active model/catalog services instance to Settings, review
and Analyze. The Settings sheet MUST use the actual shared bodies, account/key and
Stats services, server-page factory and native feedback; no silent service fallback
MAY replace them. Platform-only pages MUST be explicitly advertised and rendered by
their host, with unsupported rows absent. Before replacing credentials the root MUST
close the old settings services and their private one-time-key state. Source: Tavi's
21 Oct 2026 full same-app iOS decision, settings-is-the-liked-sheet,
client-invalidates-old-sources and the accepted thin-native-adapter plan.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] shared-stats-refresh-belongs-to-the-selected-range
Changing range or retrying MUST prevent an earlier attempt from replacing the selected
range's current summary or error. Returning to the same range before the next frame
MUST still refresh that selection, and an old scheduled producer MUST NOT gain the
replacement range's authority. Source: stats-at-once and the independent 21 Oct 2026
review preserving the original range-owned Stats state during the shared extraction.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security;product] shared-feedback-drafts-belong-to-the-source
Settings and Commands MUST use the same actual Feedback page and source-owned draft
and history. Dismissal and a failed send MUST retain unsent words; source/account/Access
retirement MUST synchronously clear words and history before replacement credentials
become usable. Old callbacks, cancelled sends and late history replies MUST NOT clear
or populate replacement state, and an older initial refresh MUST NOT replace the
post-send list. Source: nav-feedback-from-anywhere, client-invalidates-old-sources
and Tavi's 21 Oct 2026 same-app iOS request.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] settings-connection-feedback-keeps-outcome
Saving server configuration MUST distinguish a failed connection from a check replaced
by newer discovery. Supersession alone MUST NOT display an Unreachable error; an actual
failure MUST keep that attempt's recovery category rather than a later global category.
Source: Tavi's 21 Oct 2026 first-run request and review of concurrent Save/discovery.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security;product] settings-theme-choice-rechecks-its-entry-owner
A host-owned theme picker MUST reject a retired entry's retained choice, including
retirement while its theme wipe is queued. It MUST NOT change replacement preferences
or synchronize that old choice under the replacement account. Source: the accepted
22 Oct 2026 iOS Guest/private lifetime boundary and shared-commands-retire-private-owner.
